  "result": "All four tests pass.\n\n**Summary**\n\nI implemented `editor/buffer.py` with the `TextBuffer` class from the spec. Insert and delete validate their bounds and raise `IndexError` before touching the text, so a rejected call leaves the buffer unchanged. Undo and redo return `False` when their stack is empty, and any new edit clears the redo stack.\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q\n4 passed in 0.04s\n```\n\nI chose Approach A, the command pattern. Each edit is a small frozen record holding the position and the inserted or removed text, which makes the inverse trivial and keeps memory proportional to edit size rather than buffer size times history length, which matters given the spec's unbounded undo depth.",
